    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To detect text appearing inside an image, I will use the Amazon Textract service, which is a powerful tool for extracting text and data from documents. I will write a Python script that uses the Boto3 library to interact with Amazon Textract. The script will take an image file as input, call the Textract API to detect text, and print the detected text. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789889669377,
          "start": 1789889666825
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bdbcdf09002X8AaPiabrXg81s",
      "message_id": "msg_0bdbcdaf8001kzNIVpGoHwJR0T",
      "session_id": "ses_f42432519ffelERK5BfT3gjkAH",
      "time_created": 1789889666825,
      "time_updated": 1789889669377
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tooluse_i5Hz48ziNR3hD3zs5qY1B4",
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\n\ndef detect_text(image_file):\n    textract = boto3.client('textract')\n    with open(image_file, 'rb') as image:\n        image_bytes = image.read()\n    response = textract.detect_document_text(Document={'Bytes': image_bytes})\n    text = ''\n    for item in response['Blocks']:\n        if item['BlockType'] == 'LINE':\n            text += item['Text'] + ' '\n    return text\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    image_file = 'example.jpg'\n    detected_text = detect_text(image_file)\n    print(detected_text)",
            "filePath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-0f6bnpo6/detect_image_text.py"
          },
